From: port_ios lavender
Subject: [PATCH 0235] lavender: send the vsync to CoreAnimation at the panel rate (sweetfb_hz)

A spindump of backboardd on the idle lock screen (about 150 % CPU) shows the
CoreAnimation software OpenGL renderer (CA::OGL::SW: scan_convert,
image_sampler, tex_color_matrix_4x4_bias, fill_round_rect) driven by
display_timer_callback -> render_for_time.

AppleCLCD::vsyncFired notified every client at a fixed 60 Hz, while the panel
only shows a frame every fFlushTicks ticks (sweetfb_hz, 30 Hz by default in
the shim). backboardd therefore drew up to 60 frames a second on the CPU and
half of them were never displayed.

The notification now goes out only on the ticks that can flush a frame. The
internal timer stays at 60 Hz (fade, fFlushTicks accounting unchanged).

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -476,10 +476,18 @@
 	};
 
 	IOLockLock(fb->fLock);
-	for (unsigned int i = 0; i < fb->fClients->getCount(); i++) {
-		IOMobileFramebufferUserClient *client =
-		    (IOMobileFramebufferUserClient *)fb->fClients->getObject(i);
-		client->notify(SWEET_FB_NOTIFY_VSYNC, values, 6);
+	/*
+	 * 0235: the panel only shows a frame every fFlushTicks ticks
+	 * (sweetfb_hz), but backboardd draws one frame per vsync on the CPU
+	 * (CA::OGL::SW). Notifying every tick made it render 60 frames a
+	 * second of which half were never shown.
+	 */
+	if ((count % fb->fFlushTicks) == 0) {
+		for (unsigned int i = 0; i < fb->fClients->getCount(); i++) {
+			IOMobileFramebufferUserClient *client =
+			    (IOMobileFramebufferUserClient *)fb->fClients->getObject(i);
+			client->notify(SWEET_FB_NOTIFY_VSYNC, values, 6);
+		}
 	}
 	if (fb->fIntf1 != NULL && (count % 300) == 0) {
 		uint32_t frames = fb->fIntf1[(0x800 + 0x0ac) / 4];
